laurel 3041: LAUREL LOCK TIMEOUT (2994) prints its line at EARLY_BOOT, not inside kernel_startup_bootstrap(); both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/watchdog.md section 13.

[V phone 2026-11-07 04:2x, image 9ebe4fa + laurelramtop=0] With 3040 in, the boot passed "SWEET EARLY 4: cpu_bootstrap done" and stopped
before mark 5 ("kernel_startup_bootstrap done"): a blank row and two rows of dense text on the early console (sweet_early_panic: a
newline, then the panic text), no USB. Between the two marks runs kernel_startup_bootstrap(): the TUNABLES, TIMEOUTS and LOCKS phases.
2994's printf sits in ml_init_lock_timeout(), STARTUP(TIMEOUTS): printf -> os_log_with_args -> _os_log_to_msgbuf_internal ->
bsd_log_lock -> lck_ticket_lock(&log_lock); log_lock (LCK_TICKET_DECLARE in osfmk/kern/printf.c) gets its type word at STARTUP(LOCKS,
rank 4), later; the DEVELOPMENT kernel's LCK_TICKET_VERIFY sees lck_ticket_type 0, not LCK_TYPE_TICKET (0x44), and panics "Invalid
ticket lock" [I: read in the code; the photo shows the panic rows, not the words]. The kill switch laurellockto=0 printed its "off"
line from the same place. A good boot's first printf is "iBoot version" (PE_init_platform(TRUE), after kernel_startup_bootstrap()).
Fix: the decision and the timeouts stay at TIMEOUTS (they must hold from the first contended lock); the line prints from
STARTUP(EARLY_BOOT, STARTUP_RANK_LAST, laurel_lock_timeout_line), where LAUREL RAM prints too. Host test: scripts/laurel/test-early-lines.sh.

diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
